<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Nasir (Abbasid caliph)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1180–1225</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Nasir was an Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> who reigned from 1180 to 1225. He sought to restore the political power of the caliphate in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> after a long period of domination by Seljuk sultans, using diplomacy and religious networks. His reign raised brief hopes of a genuine Abbasid revival, but the caliphate fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> in 1258.</p></div>
